#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:4
msgid "Cambricon MLU Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:6
msgid ""
"The MLU backend implements the community ``DeviceSpec`` and ``DeviceOps``"
" interfaces for multiprocess **engine-driven** transfers. It uses "
"``torch_mlu`` tensor operations to move KV blocks between MLU memory and "
"canonical host chunks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:12
msgid "Requirements and selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:14
msgid ""
"Install a matching Cambricon driver, Neuware runtime, PyTorch, and "
"``torch_mlu`` distribution first. Build LMCache's common C++ extensions "
"against that PyTorch installation, without GPU-specific extensions::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:20
msgid ""
"Use an environment with the repository's build dependencies installed. Do"
" not replace the vendor's PyTorch version as part of this installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:23
msgid "Set these variables before starting the serving engine::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"The backend probes ``torch_mlu`` at startup. Explicit selection fails if "
"the runtime is missing or no MLU is available. A CPU-only LMCache server "
"does not need ``LMCACHE_DEVICE_BACKEND=mlu``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:33
msgid "Supported transfer contract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:35
msgid ""
"The MP serving adapter must pass real per-layer MLU tensors and an "
"accurate ``kv_layout`` hint. The supported layouts are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:38
msgid "K/V-first NHD: ``[2, num_blocks, block_size, num_heads, head_size]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:39
msgid "K/V-first HND: ``[2, num_blocks, num_heads, block_size, head_size]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:40
msgid "MLA: ``[num_blocks, block_size, head_size]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:42
msgid ""
"The vLLM adapter normalizes legacy MLU layout queries to HND, matching "
"Cambricon's V1 FlashAttention allocation. Explicitly resolved layouts "
"from newer vLLM versions retain their reported value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:46
msgid ""
"Host chunks use the same token-major layout as other community backends. "
"Callers must synchronize the transfer stream before consuming host chunks"
" or releasing their storage. Completion recorders wait synchronously for "
"the supplied MLU queue before publishing completion. The zero handle "
"denotes ``torch.mlu.default_stream()`` on the current device. A nonzero "
"handle borrows the caller's stream; the caller retains ownership and must"
" keep the stream alive until the call returns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:54
msgid ""
"The MP transfer context owns source and destination tensors until gather "
"completion. Error recovery and request-level completion tracking belong "
"to the shared context and worker adapter. This device backend does not "
"modify those lifecycle mechanisms or establish end-to-end preemption "
"safety."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:59
msgid ""
"D2H copies into non-contiguous host slices also block. This preserves "
"correctness for prefix skips on torch_mlu versions where an asynchronous "
"strided D2H copy can return incorrect data even after synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:63
msgid ""
"This backend does not add a vLLM-MLU serving connector. In particular, it"
" does not implement the vendor connector's remote-allocation extensions. "
"A serving adapter must use the community MP engine-driven interface. V1 "
"support alone does not establish connector compatibility: the serving "
"runtime must also provide the vLLM APIs used by the installed LMCache "
"connector. A passing device transfer test does not validate those APIs. "
"Serving adapters must finish pending gathers before KV block reuse, "
"consume flush metadata before retrieval and forward, and wait for pending"
" host-to-server commits before closing. Request-level completion receipts"
" remain the responsibility of the shared worker adapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:75
msgid "Capability limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"Raw pointer transfers, the legacy in-process connector, LMCache-driven "
"IPC, arbitrary host-memory registration, and native transfer kernels are "
"not supported. Unsupported transfer entry points raise errors instead of "
"treating MLU addresses as host pointers. ``auto`` selects "
"``engine_driven``. This implementation makes no throughput or latency "
"guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:84
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:86
msgid "Run the backend tests in the configured MLU environment::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:91
msgid ""
"The transfer matrix runs on both CPU and MLU. MLU cases skip when no "
"usable runtime is present; skipped cases are not hardware validation. The"
" tests exercise layout correctness and MP gather/scatter dispatch, not "
"full model serving."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:96
msgid ""
"For full serving validation, check KV bit equality across store and "
"restore separately from generated tokens and log probabilities. Compare "
"the warm request with native prefix reuse at the same hit length: full "
"prefill and partial prefill may use different numerical paths. Repeated "
"runs and an explicit synchronization control help distinguish numerical "
"differences from stream-ordering failures; a log-probability tolerance "
"alone does not establish transfer correctness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/platform/devices/mlu/index.rst:104
msgid ""
"Also match the batch timeline: co-scheduled requests, remaining query "
"lengths, and batch order can change the model's numerical path. To "
"isolate this effect, replay a captured timeline with identical prefix KV "
"in an engine without an LMCache connector. Compare logits before sampling"
" and replay fixed logits separately. Greedy decoding can produce "
"different tokens when batch-dependent rounding changes two nearly tied "
"logits; a fixed seed does not establish batch-invariant model "
"computation."
msgstr ""

